<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Raghuji III Bhonsle</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1808">1808</a>–<a href="/years/1853">1853</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Raghuji III Bhonsle was the last <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/maratha-empire">Maratha</a> raja of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nagpur">Nagpur</a>, placed on the throne as a boy in 1818 after the deposition of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mudhoji-ii-bhonsle">Appa Sahib</a> and kept under close British supervision during his minority. When he died in 1853 without a son or adopted heir, Governor-General <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lord-dalhousie">Lord Dalhousie</a> annexed the kingdom under the doctrine of lapse, and it became the British <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nagpur-province">Nagpur Province</a>.</p></div>
